      "description": "Watch Coventry City vs Aston Villa highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 16, 2026. On September 16, 2026 , Coventry City hosted Aston Villa in a high-stakes Carabao Cup encounter. Both sides took to the pitch with clear attacking intent, looking to secure their progression in the tournament under the floodlights. Early Exchanges and the Opening Blow Aston Villa wasted no time establishing their dominance, breaking the deadlock in the 7th minute. Tammy Abraham found the bottom right corner with a clinical right-footed finish following a perfectly weighted through ball from George Hemmings . Coventry City faced an early setback when Aurèle Amenda was forced off with an injury, replaced by Ethan Pinnock , but the hosts refused to crumble under the pressure. Their persistence paid off in the 27th minute when Victor Torp curled a magnificent free kick into the top right corner to level the scores. Villa Reclaim the Lead As the first half drew to a close, Aston Villa intensified their pressure. In the 40th minute, a corner routine proved decisive as Ibrahim Mbaye delivered a cross for Ross Barkley , who rose highest to plant a header into the bottom left corner. The visitors suffered a blow of their own just before the break, as goalkeeper Marco Bizot was forced off due to injury, handing Zion Suzuki his opportunity between the posts. Abraham Seals the Victory The second half saw Aston Villa tighten their grip on the match. In the 59th minute, Tammy Abraham secured his second goal of the night, converting from close range after an assist from Ross Barkley following yet another corner. Coventry City attempted a late rally through chances from Victor Torp and Loum Tchaouna , but the Premier League side remained composed. Despite late yellow cards for Emiliano Buendía and Frank Onyeka , the match concluded with a 3-1 victory for the visitors, confirming their place in the next round."
